Good, I have a clear picture of the button patterns. Now let me create the shared Button component. Per the Codex review, I should do an incremental migration — create the component and migrate 1-2 screens. Let me create the Button component with the most common variants: primary, secondary, text, and danger.

Let me design the component:

```typescript
type ButtonVariant = 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'text' | 'danger';
type ButtonSize = 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg';

interface ButtonProps extends React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement> {
  variant?: ButtonVariant;
  size?: ButtonSize;
  loading?: boolean;
  href?: string; // renders as <a> when provided
}
```

Now I'm defining the styling for each variant — primary gets the brand colors with hover states and disabled styling, secondary uses a bordered white approach with gray backgrounds on hover, and text is minimal with just color changes.

Adding the danger variant for destructive actions and then mapping out the size options from small to large with their respective padding and text sizes.

